-- lib/search.cub — search over a text by its suffixes, sharded by each suffix's first token (Avik,
-- 2026-11-18: "load all suffixes into a trie and it serves"; every process local, so a query reads one
-- shard and no process holds a corpus). A text is lowered and tokenized (lib/repeats.cub, tokenize,
-- with tokenize-content); every point of it begins a suffix. hits q i ts is the specification: every
-- point of ts, numbered from i, at which the token sequence q begins. shard k i ts is the shard: the
-- suffixes whose first token's first two bytes are k, each with its point. search q i ts reads only the
-- shard of q's first token. search-ok: search q i ts is hits q i ts, for every query and every text.
import "repeats.cub"

